[{"id":2497312883,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6U2fhz","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?u=96b5dc9be2859dca5f31314c87d99a68a21e1576&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","login":"BastiaanOlij","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij"},"body":"@DarioSamo or @clayjohn can probably judge a little better whether the extra loop would have an unwanted impact and whether there is a more efficient way to do this but as in reality it's unlikely that more than 2, maybe 3, probes overlap I think it's fine.\r\n\r\nMy only question would be whether this should be an option, not always applied. Personally I've never had very good results with the current approach of just blending all overlapping probes so I'm not overly concerned that this new logic is the new way of doing it, but there might be users who wish the use the old form of blending.\r\n\r\nOther than that. I think this is a great improvement. It could use a video showing it in action, the animations with the colored probes show well how things are working but seeing the actual end result showing a good use case, would help convince people why this is worth it.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100241#pullrequestreview-2497312883","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100241","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2024-12-12T00:37:56Z"},{"id":2499062573,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6U9Kst","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?u=fbd6cc58970fe319828923ed6ba1d88f03338d59&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","login":"lander-vr","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100241#pullrequestreview-2499062573","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100241","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2024-12-12T11:24:45Z"},{"id":2506892382,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6VbCRe","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally (rebased on top of `master` https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/08508d2e01567446ef7cf721b39041a51e2eddfd), it works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_100241.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18154699/test_pr_100241.zip)\r\n\r\n## Comparison\r\n\r\nVisually, it's quite different in Forward+, but it's almost the same in Mobile. Is the visual difference intended? I'd expect Forward+ to look as close as possible to Mobile, like it did before.\r\n\r\n### Forward+\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n![Screenshot_20241216_184909 png webp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cdd35cf4-376c-4a06-824a-54888dd673e3) | ![Screenshot_20241216_184930 png webp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b07f2ae7-e4b5-4dd3-a8f2-26633969d45b)\r\n\r\n### Mobile\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n![Screenshot_20241216_184915 png webp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4168382a-c5b9-42d6-970a-7414928fcbcd) | ![Screenshot_20241216_184939 png webp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/61113ac0-d5d3-43e1-97ef-34e980e73de4)\r\n\r\n## Benchmark\r\n\r\n<details open>\r\n\r\n<summary>PC specifications</summary>\r\n\r\n- **CPU:** Intel Core i9-13900K\r\n- **GPU:** NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090\r\n- **RAM:** 64 GB (2×32 GB DDR5-5800 C30)\r\n- **SSD:** Solidigm P44 Pro 2 TB\r\n- **OS:** Linux (Fedora 41)\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nAll tests done in 3840×2160.\r\n\r\n### Before\r\n\r\nForward+ | Mobile | Compatibility[^1]\r\n-|-|-\r\n1151 FPS (0.87 mspf) | 1753 FPS (0.57 mspf) | 3915 FPS (0.25 mspf)\r\n\r\n### After\r\n\r\nForward+ | Mobile | Compatibility[^1]\r\n-|-|-\r\n1278 FPS (0.78 mspf) | 2896 FPS (0.34 mspf) | 3903 FPS (0.25 mspf)\r\n\r\n[^1]: Only 2 probes per mesh can be rendered, so some of them were skipped during rendering.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100241#pullrequestreview-2506892382","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100241","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-12-16T17:51:19Z"},{"id":2512778765,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6VxfYN","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100241#pullrequestreview-2512778765","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100241","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-12-18T20:25:42Z"},{"id":25